<p style=3D"font-size:16px; line-height:175%"><span style=3D"font-family: L=
ato, Tahoma, sans-serif;">A widespread Cloudflare outage on Tuesday tempora=
rily knocked major websites offline, including X, OpenAI, Letterboxd, and p=
arts of League of Legends. Users saw =E2=80=9Cinternal server error=E2=80=
=9D messages tied to Cloudflare=E2=80=99s network, and even outage tracker =
Down Detector struggled to load due to the same underlying issue.</span></p=
>
<p style=3D"font-size:16px; line-height:175%"><span style=3D"font-family: L=
ato, Tahoma, sans-serif;">The disruption began around 11:30 a.m. UK time, w=
ith Cloudflare acknowledging the issue minutes later. Early updates indicat=
ed widespread 500 errors impacting multiple customers, the Cloudflare dashb=
oard, and the company=E2=80=99s API. While Cloudflare didn=E2=80=99t immedi=
ately identify the cause, later statements said services were gradually rec=
overing, though higher-than-normal error rates might persist during remedia=
tion.</span></p>
<p style=3D"font-size:16px; line-height:175%"><span style=3D"font-family: L=
ato, Tahoma, sans-serif;">Cloudflare, which sits behind a massive portion o=
f global internet traffic, typically operates invisibly =E2=80=94 handling =
security, routing, and uptime for millions of sites. Outages of this scale =
echo the AWS incident a month earlier, where a single provider issue cascad=
ed across unrelated services. By early afternoon, some major platforms had =
begun loading again, though Cloudflare had not yet declared the incident fu=
lly resolved.</span></p>
<p style=3D"font-size:16px; line-height:175%"><span style=3D"font-family: L=
ato, Tahoma, sans-serif;">So if your website (or a site you tried to visit)=
 blinked out today, chances are it wasn=E2=80=99t you. It was Cloudflare ta=
king an unplanned break.</span></p>
